(Bugs #72 and #91 composed. A miss yields the NUMBER 0 at the read, whatever
 the collection holds; it is the destination that re-types it. Where the miss
 is provable #72 refuses a pointer destination outright, so every pointer row
 below is an unprovable miss. A `number` destination must never be handed the
 element type's empty value - that was the composition defect this pins.)

(A provable miss out of a list of TEXT, read into a number: the number 0.)
a list called words is ["a", "b"].
a number called 'missing word' is element 5 of words.
Print 'missing word'.

(The same where the miss is NOT provable - an Append means the length is no
 longer known - still the number 0.)
a list called grown is ["a", "b"].
Append "c" to grown.
a number called 'missing grown' is element 5 of grown.
Print 'missing grown'.

(An unprovable miss into a TEXT destination: the empty text, not the raw 0,
 so the first read does not dereference null.)
a text called 'missing text' is element 5 of grown.
Print "[{'missing text'}]".

(A tagless consumer has no declared destination and reads the value as the
 list's element type. Print, a format hole, and an append each get the empty
 text rather than the 0.)
Print element 5 of grown.
Print "[{element 5 of grown}]".
a list called collected is [].
Append element 5 of grown to collected.
Print collected.

(first/last of an empty list miss the same way, by the same two rules.)
a list called blank is [].
a number called 'no first' is blank's first.
Print 'no first'.

(The error flag is untouched by any of it.)
a number called probe is element 9 of grown.
On error print "error flag still fires".
Exit 0.
